%% Reprise - fix assistance and verification
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor M as Maintainer
    participant GH as GitHub
    participant E as Engine
    participant B as Bob (agent mode, no execute)
    participant S as Sandbox

    M->>GH: comment /reprise fix on issue N (CONFIRMED or FLAKY)
    GH->>E: issue_comment event
    E->>E: trust check, load record, create branch reprise/fix-N from default branch
    E->>E: add repro test from record to workspace
    loop iteration 1..3
        E->>B: propose-fix prompt (+ previous results on --resume)
        B-->>E: edits in src/** or test/** + JSON summary
        E->>E: revert out-of-scope edits, reject if repro test changed
        E->>S: quick check: repro test x3, full suite x1
        S-->>E: results
        alt repro passes and no new failures
            E->>E: stop loop
        end
    end
    E->>GH: push branch, open draft PR "Fixes #N" with best candidate + repro test
    E->>S: full verification (repro runs = required n, regression compare vs base)
    S-->>E: results
    E->>GH: PR comment + label FIX_VERIFIED / FIX_INCOMPLETE / REGRESSION_DETECTED
    E->>GH: update issue comment and record, redeploy dashboard

    Note over M,GH: A developer can instead open their own PR with "Fixes #N".
    M->>GH: push to PR or /reprise verify
    GH->>E: pull_request event
    E->>S: same verification (repro test injected from record if absent)
    E->>GH: PR comment + label
